{"vid":"Y5vLiBz7oeQ","source":"Y5vLiBz7oeQ.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"With gas metal arc welding, there's a"},{"t":2,"txt":"lot happening down at the arc. I'm going"},{"t":4,"txt":"to break it all down for you."},{"t":6,"txt":"Hey, welcome to the shop. So, a"},{"t":7.5,"txt":"fundamental understanding of how the arc"},{"t":9.9,"txt":"works and what's going on down there is"},{"t":12,"txt":"going to make it much easier for you to"},{"t":13.4,"txt":"get your settings dialed in and get a"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"good weld. Now, what actually happens"},{"t":17.8,"txt":"there depends on a number of factors,"},{"t":19.7,"txt":"the type of machine you're using, what"},{"t":21.4,"txt":"your shielding gas is, where your"},{"t":22.9,"txt":"settings are at. First of all, let's"},{"t":24.6,"txt":"look at the one that is used by 90% of"},{"t":28,"txt":"people. If you're MIG welding, you're"},{"t":29.9,"txt":"probably welding in this way. What that"},{"t":32.5,"txt":"is is the short circuit transfer mode."},{"t":35.5,"txt":"In other parts of the world, it's called"},{"t":36.7,"txt":"the dip transfer mode. Now, what's"},{"t":39,"txt":"happening here is your arc isn't going"},{"t":41.3,"txt":"all the time. The arc actually goes out"},{"t":44.4,"txt":"over and over again, and that is why you"},{"t":46.8,"txt":"get that crackling or frying bacon"},{"t":49,"txt":"sound."},{"t":52.3,"txt":"The wire feeds in, touches your"},{"t":54.6,"txt":"material, and then it burns back like a"},{"t":56.9,"txt":"fuse blowing. When that happens, it"},{"t":59.2,"txt":"starts an arc. That's where the"},{"t":61,"txt":"electricity is bridging a gap there, and"},{"t":64.1,"txt":"it produces a tremendous amount of heat."},{"t":66.9,"txt":"Well, as this is happening, that arc is"},{"t":69.2,"txt":"actually melting the wire, and it's"},{"t":71.5,"txt":"melting the wire faster than the wire's"},{"t":73.8,"txt":"coming out of the gun, so the arc gets"},{"t":75.3,"txt":"longer and longer and longer until there"},{"t":77.1,"txt":"isn't enough voltage left to keep that"},{"t":79.3,"txt":"arc going, and it goes out. The wire's"},{"t":81.6,"txt":"still feeding out, it'll go down and"},{"t":83.5,"txt":"touch your material, and repeat that"},{"t":85.2,"txt":"process over and over again many times"},{"t":87.4,"txt":"per second. Now, you might be scratching"},{"t":89.6,"txt":"your head wondering, why would we do"},{"t":91.2,"txt":"that whole song and dance? You know,"},{"t":93.4,"txt":"when you're stick welding or when you're"},{"t":94.8,"txt":"TIG welding, the arc is going all the"},{"t":96.6,"txt":"time. Why would we want to have this"},{"t":98.9,"txt":"short circuit transfer mode? Well, the"},{"t":101,"txt":"reality is in MIG welding, there is"},{"t":103.5,"txt":"another version where you keep the arc"},{"t":105.8,"txt":"going all the time. We'll talk about it"},{"t":107.4,"txt":"in a minute, but the reason why you'd"},{"t":110.2,"txt":"want to use this short circuit transfer"},{"t":112.4,"txt":"mode to have the arc only lit part of"},{"t":114.3,"txt":"the time is because it helps to regulate"},{"t":117.1,"txt":"the amount of heat that you're putting"},{"t":118.8,"txt":"in or the rate that heat is going into"},{"t":121.1,"txt":"your material because that arc isn't"},{"t":123.7,"txt":"always on. And this lets you do things"},{"t":126.5,"txt":"like weld thinner material. It lets you"},{"t":128.4,"txt":"do things like weld in the vertical and"},{"t":130.3,"txt":"overhead position and also makes it"},{"t":132.9,"txt":"possible for lower amperage machines"},{"t":136.1,"txt":"like your 110 volt machines to be able"},{"t":138.4,"txt":"to work. Well, let's shift gears here"},{"t":140.7,"txt":"and talk about the spray transfer mode."},{"t":143.9,"txt":"And that's where your arc is lit all the"},{"t":146.1,"txt":"time. Now, in order to run this, you"},{"t":147.6,"txt":"need to have a machine that can output"},{"t":149.9,"txt":"sufficient current and voltage and you"},{"t":151.8,"txt":"also need to change your gas from a 25%"},{"t":155.6,"txt":"CO2 down to like a 10% CO2 gas to run"},{"t":159.1,"txt":"spray transfer or sometimes you'll"},{"t":161.7,"txt":"actually run almost straight argon with"},{"t":163.9,"txt":"just a percent or two of oxygen in it."},{"t":166.1,"txt":"With spray transfer mode, you're keeping"},{"t":169,"txt":"your arc lit all the time and the length"},{"t":171.9,"txt":"of that arc actually depends on your"},{"t":174.6,"txt":"voltage setting. Turn up voltage, you"},{"t":176.8,"txt":"get a longer arc and then your cone will"},{"t":179.8,"txt":"spray out further off of there with the"},{"t":181.8,"txt":"metal coming off of your wire in really"},{"t":184.5,"txt":"fine droplets. Welding with spray"},{"t":186.5,"txt":"transfer has some real advantages. First"},{"t":188.8,"txt":"of all, you can put down a lot of"},{"t":190.2,"txt":"material in a hurry with spray transfer."},{"t":192.9,"txt":"Second, when you're welding on thicker"},{"t":194.8,"txt":"material, it actually gives you better"},{"t":196.9,"txt":"penetration and can help avoid things"},{"t":200.2,"txt":"like lack of fusion defects. And because"},{"t":202.9,"txt":"that arc is going all the time, much"},{"t":205.4,"txt":"less spatter and you know, much less of"},{"t":207.9,"txt":"an erratic arc coming off of there and"},{"t":210.1,"txt":"it lays in nice and smooth. However,"},{"t":212.2,"txt":"like we talked about before, it's just"},{"t":214.4,"txt":"dumping a ton of heat in non-stop. And"},{"t":218.2,"txt":"so, you can't do things like weld"},{"t":220.3,"txt":"vertically or overhead or in other"},{"t":223.2,"txt":"positions and you can't really use it on"},{"t":225.4,"txt":"thinner material. In between short"},{"t":227.5,"txt":"circuit transfer and spray transfer,"},{"t":230,"txt":"there is kind of a middle ground called"},{"t":231.8,"txt":"globular transfer where your metal come"},{"t":234,"txt":"off in larger droplets. It's less"},{"t":236.6,"txt":"commonly the target of what you're"},{"t":238.2,"txt":"trying to get to though it does have"},{"t":239.7,"txt":"some uses. Well, you might be wondering"},{"t":241.9,"txt":"here we are in 2022, isn't there some"},{"t":245.1,"txt":"version that gives you the best of both"},{"t":247.9,"txt":"worlds? There is, but you need a pretty"},{"t":249.8,"txt":"fancy machine to do it."},{"t":252,"txt":"What you have here is pulsed spray"},{"t":255.1,"txt":"transfer or pulsed MIG."},{"t":257.5,"txt":"Now, what's happening with pulsed MIG is"},{"t":260,"txt":"rather than relying on the physics of"},{"t":261.9,"txt":"that short circuit transfer mode to turn"},{"t":264.5,"txt":"your weld on and off and on and off,"},{"t":267,"txt":"you're using electronics or computer to"},{"t":269.8,"txt":"turn the voltage and current up and down"},{"t":272.1,"txt":"and up and down. And when you do that,"},{"t":274.4,"txt":"you're able to regulate that heat while"},{"t":276.8,"txt":"still keeping the arc lit all the time."},{"t":279.1,"txt":"This gives you the better penetration"},{"t":281.4,"txt":"and the smoother arc that you'd have"},{"t":284,"txt":"with a spray transfer and eliminates a"},{"t":286,"txt":"lot of the spatter that you'd get. And"},{"t":288.3,"txt":"it also regulates your heat input you to"},{"t":291.5,"txt":"weld out of position or on thinner"},{"t":293.7,"txt":"materials. With all these variations of"},{"t":295.8,"txt":"the process, there are a few things in"},{"t":297.9,"txt":"common. One is that you're using a"},{"t":301.2,"txt":"constant voltage power supply. Now, this"},{"t":304.9,"txt":"is different from the power supply that"},{"t":307.3,"txt":"you'd use for stick welding or TIG"},{"t":309.1,"txt":"welding, which are called constant"},{"t":311.1,"txt":"current supplies and they try to"},{"t":312.6,"txt":"maintain the same amperage. That's why"},{"t":314.2,"txt":"you set amps when you're stick welding"},{"t":316,"txt":"or TIG welding. And here with MIG"},{"t":317.8,"txt":"welding, we're setting volts."},{"t":319.8,"txt":"Now, you use a constant voltage power"},{"t":321.8,"txt":"supply because your voltage really"},{"t":324.8,"txt":"regulates the length of your arc. So,"},{"t":327.6,"txt":"when you go to a higher voltage, you're"},{"t":329.2,"txt":"going to get a longer arc. A lower"},{"t":331,"txt":"voltage will give you a shorter one."},{"t":333.2,"txt":"Now, because the machine is trying to"},{"t":335.8,"txt":"maintain the same voltage, and it"},{"t":337.3,"txt":"doesn't maintain the exact same voltage,"},{"t":339.2,"txt":"but uh you know, that's the goal is for"},{"t":342.1,"txt":"this machine to maintain the same"},{"t":344.4,"txt":"voltage. When you increase your wire"},{"t":346.8,"txt":"feed speed, and you're dumping wire in"},{"t":349.1,"txt":"there faster, it has to automatically"},{"t":352.3,"txt":"increase your welding current or"},{"t":354.4,"txt":"amperage to be able to keep the same"},{"t":357.4,"txt":"voltage going. That's why increasing"},{"t":360,"txt":"your wire feed speed is going to"},{"t":361.7,"txt":"increase the amount of heat you get in"},{"t":363.4,"txt":"your part, because it increases the"},{"t":365.2,"txt":"amperage or current that goes into your"},{"t":366.9,"txt":"part. So, that's why you'll see on your"},{"t":370.8,"txt":"charts, when you go to thicker material,"},{"t":373.2,"txt":"you go to a higher wire feed speed, cuz"},{"t":375.4,"txt":"it gives you more current. And you need"},{"t":377.3,"txt":"to change your voltage, as well, to be"},{"t":379.4,"txt":"able to maintain the ratio of wire feed"},{"t":381.8,"txt":"speed and voltage to control your actual"},{"t":385,"txt":"amperage. So, if you want to know more"},{"t":387.5,"txt":"about the details of setting your"},{"t":389.3,"txt":"machine and getting that all dialed in,"},{"t":391.3,"txt":"I have a video all about that you can"},{"t":393,"txt":"check out here. Thanks for tuning in"},{"t":395.2,"txt":"today. We'll see you next time."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"With"